cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "JOSSeph: A Docker-first pipeline for extracting metrics from Java open-source repositories"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-04-02"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chesnokoff/oss-metrics"
abstract: >
  JOSSeph is a reproducible, Docker-first pipeline for extracting multi-dimensional
  quality metrics from GitHub Java repositories. It integrates four metrics sources:
  CK (static object-oriented metrics), CM (change/process metrics), the GitHub REST API
  (project metadata), and SonarQube (maintainability and reliability measures). JOSSeph
  is designed for empirical software engineering research that requires reproducible,
  artifact-verified metric extraction at scale.
keywords:
  - empirical software engineering
  - software metrics
  - static analysis
  - repository mining
  - Java
  - reproducibility
authors:
  - family-names: Chesnokov
    given-names: Aleksandr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2772-4881"
